<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Provisional Government of Western Thrace</h1><p class="st-meta">1913 CE – 1913 CE · capital Komotini</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived Muslim-led state in Western Thrace in 1913, set up by Ottoman officers to keep the region from Bulgaria after the Second Balkan War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-thrace">Western Thrace</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a>. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-balkan-war">Second Balkan War</a> broke out in 1913, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edirne">Edirne</a>, and Ottoman officers led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleyman-askeri">Süleyman Askerî</a>, together with local Turkish and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomaks">Pomak</a> irregulars, drove Bulgarian forces from the region. In late August 1913 they proclaimed an independent government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/komotini">Gümülcine</a>, today Komotini.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government had a president, ministers, a flag, stamps and an army of a few thousand irregulars, drawing on the region's Muslim majority. It was effectively run by Ottoman officers acting unofficially, and no foreign power recognised it. It lasted about two months.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By the Treaty of Constantinople in September 1913 the Ottoman government recognised Bulgarian possession of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-thrace">Western Thrace</a> and withdrew support, and Bulgarian troops took over in October. The region passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, where its Muslim minority remains.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/provisional-government-of-western-thrace.jpg" alt="Provisional Government of Western Thrace" width="320" height="217"><figcaption>Image: Darwinek · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_TRWT.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1913 CE – 1913 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Komotini</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Süleyman Askerî</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Turkish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gumuljina Republic, Independent Government of Western Thrace</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1913&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-western-thrace" aria-label="Provisional Government of Western Thrace on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5301 711 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Provisional Government of Western Thrace lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5621 967L5564 916"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5564 916h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5621 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5621 967h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1913&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-western-thrace">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

